    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d722">

                <pb facs="0993" n="979" sameAs="frus:frus1944v06/pg979"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.24/11–244</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by President Roosevelt to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-11-02">November 2,
                        1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>As you know, the Russians have recently granted us permission to transport 500
                    trucks across Russia to China. I recommend that you personally cable Marshal
                        Stalin,<anchor n="29" xml:id="d722-f1"/> asking permission to transport a
                    further 500 trucks per month over Russian territory for China.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>F[<hi rendition="#small-caps">ranklin</hi>] D. R[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">oosevelt</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d722-f1" n="29" xml:id="d722-f1-content">
                <p>Iosif Vissarionovich Stalin, Chairman of the Council of Commissars of the Soviet
                    Union.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
